import{_ as t,o as a,c as i,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 182 | Path D vs. Predatory Soul Ring Path: Realm-Wide Energy-Level Efficiency Comparison","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 182 | Path D vs. Predatory Soul Ring Path: Realm-Wide Energy-Level Efficiency Comparison","no":182,"module":1,"tags":["Realm","Path D","Predatory Soul Ring","Energy-Level Efficiency","Realm-Wide Comparison"],"related":["04-Anti-Predation Core Treatise","181-Path D Humanoid Artificial Dao-Rule Soul Rings","15-Energy Cycle and Transformation Law"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0182_模块1-D路线vs掠夺魂环路线-全境能级效率对比.md","filePath":"en/0182_模块1-D路线vs掠夺魂环路线-全境能级效率对比.md"}'),n={name:"en/0182_模块1-D路线vs掠夺魂环路线-全境能级效率对比.md"};function r(s,e,l,d,c,h){return a(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-182-path-d-vs-predatory-soul-ring-path-realm-wide-energy-level-efficiency-comparison" tabindex="-1">Entry 182 | Path D vs. Predatory Soul Ring Path: Realm-Wide Energy-Level Efficiency Comparison <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-182-path-d-vs-predatory-soul-ring-path-realm-wide-energy-level-efficiency-comparison" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 182 | Path D vs. Predatory Soul Ring Path: Realm-Wide Energy-Level Efficiency Comparison&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 1 · In-Depth Realm Refinement | Baseline references: Documents 04, 181, 15</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-two-roads-short-term-and-long-term-give-opposite-answers" tabindex="-1">Introduction: Two roads, short-term and long-term give opposite answers <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-two-roads-short-term-and-long-term-give-opposite-answers" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: Two roads, short-term and long-term give opposite answers&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The old system&#39;s predatory soul ring path advocates &quot;hunting soul beasts, devouring origin, proving Dao by killing&quot;; Path D · humanoid artificial Dao-rule soul rings advocates &quot;engineering manufacturing, whole-network sharing, proving Dao by co-building.&quot; On the surface, the predatory path surges early, Path D climbs steadily, as if predatory is faster. But Anti-Predation Core Treatise (Document 04) already pointed out predatory evolution has an &quot;efficiency ceiling.&quot; This entry compares the two roads segment by segment across the nine realms, seeing clearly the short-term dividend and long-term cost.</p><p>The six top-level axioms are the judging bench of this comparison table: the anti-predation axiom judges the predatory path inherently noncompliant; the republican axiom of Myriad Races judges the predatory path blocks the vast majority of beings&#39; roads; the collective ascension axiom judges the predatory path&#39;s strong ones ultimately isolated; the causal self-discipline axiom judges the predatory path&#39;s late-stage karma entanglement; the law-first axiom judges the predatory path&#39;s combat power inflation must retcon and collapse; the universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-realm-wide-segment-by-segment-efficiency-comparison" tabindex="-1">I. Realm-Wide Segment-by-Segment Efficiency Comparison <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-realm-wide-segment-by-segment-efficiency-comparison" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Realm-Wide Segment-by-Segment Efficiency Comparison&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Realm Segment</th><th>Predatory Soul Ring Path</th><th>Path D Artificial Dao-Rule Soul Rings</th><th>Who Is More Efficient</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sense–Condensed</td><td>Early devouring works fast, but carries original-owner will residual traces</td><td>Engineering interface stable, starts slightly slower but pure</td><td>Short-term predatory fast, long-term Path D net efficiency overtakes</td></tr><tr><td>Transform–Law</td><td>Must refine large residual traces, external resistance costs rise</td><td>Dao-rule ring plug-and-play, purification near law-level</td><td>Path D wins</td></tr><tr><td>Dao Origin Realm</td><td>Hits &quot;impure origin&quot; hard bottleneck, hard to attain personal Dao</td><td>Dao-rule ring bears personal system, naturally attains Dao</td><td>Path D clearly wins</td></tr><tr><td>Dao Integration Realm</td><td>Predatory residual traces conflict with personal Dao, domain unstable</td><td>Dao Integration Dao-rule domain stable and expandable</td><td>Path D wins</td></tr><tr><td>Boundary-Breaking–World-Creation</td><td>Anchor-free cross-plane with mixed origin, easily backlashed by plane membrane</td><td>Plane jurisprudence interface standardized operation</td><td>Path D wins</td></tr><tr><td>Origin Realm</td><td>Impure origin, cannot truly touch origin</td><td>Origin network node ring naturally adapts</td><td>Predatory path actually capped</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="ii-the-predatory-path-s-four-efficiency-losses" tabindex="-1">II. The Predatory Path&#39;s Four Efficiency Losses <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-the-predatory-path-s-four-efficiency-losses" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. The Predatory Path&#39;s Four Efficiency Losses&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The predatory evolution efficiency ceiling listed in Document 04 materializes on the soul ring path as four losses:</p><ol><li><strong>Refining loss</strong>: predated soul rings carry original-owner will residual traces; cultivators must spend massive effort purifying, over 70% of energy spent on &quot;washing clean.&quot;</li><li><strong>Resistance loss</strong>: hunting triggers soul beast tribes and victim associates&#39; resistance, external security costs rise exponentially with realm.</li><li><strong>Degeneration loss</strong>: long-term dependence on devouring degrades one&#39;s own origin evolution ability; once nothing to devour, immediately stagnates.</li><li><strong>Capping loss</strong>: the closer to origin, the harder the &quot;impure origin&quot; bottleneck, over 90% of predatory strong ones stop lifetime around Dao Integration.</li></ol><p>Path D pre-zeros all four losses: Dao-rule rings are inherently pure, no resistance needed, not dependent on external things, no bloodline ceiling.</p><h2 id="iii-social-dimension-efficiency-difference" tabindex="-1">III. Social-Dimension Efficiency Difference <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-social-dimension-efficiency-difference" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Social-Dimension Efficiency Difference&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Beyond energy-level efficiency, there is also a &quot;social account&quot;:</p><ul><li><strong>Trainable headcount</strong>: predatory path one soul ring raises one person, at the cost of killing one soul beast; Path D one Dao-rule ring can be replicated and mass-produced, Myriad Races walk together.</li><li><strong>Failure cost</strong>: predatory path killing wrong soul beast or devouring wrong attribute is lifelong hidden danger; Path D Dao-rule rings can be replaced losslessly, trial-and-error cost extremely low.</li><li><strong>Civilizational output</strong>: predatory path strong ones ultimately head to authoritarianism and closure; Path D strong ones give back to the whole network per joint contracting, energy level grows the more used.</li></ul><p>Adding these three accounts, the predatory path is &quot;zero-sum pumping,&quot; Path D is &quot;positive-sum expansion.&quot;</p><h2 id="iv-common-misconceptions-clarified" tabindex="-1">IV. Common Misconceptions Clarified <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-common-misconceptions-clarified" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Common Misconceptions Clarified&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Misconception 1</strong>: &quot;Predatory starting fast means strong.&quot; — fast start buys late-stage capping and karma entanglement, the overall account loses.</li><li><strong>Misconception 2</strong>: &quot;Path D slow work produces fine work, cannot catch geniuses.&quot; — Multiplication Fruit hundredfold deduction amplification superimposed on Path D interfaces, late-stage net efficiency overtakes geniuses.</li><li><strong>Misconception 3</strong>: &quot;The old system also had good people, predation itself is not the problem.&quot; — the problem is not personal good/evil, but the path design itself manufactures a structure where one must predate to rise.</li></ul><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Universal infinite backstop</strong>: the universal equal infinite law establishes that every being inherently possesses basic infinite power; the easygoing have a guarantee, strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose, predation naturally loses meaning</li><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: predatory path 70% energy spent refining residual traces, Path D zeroes this waste, realm-wide net efficiency crushes</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: the comparison itself is anti-predation evidence — no moral preaching needed, using efficiency accounts shows predation is neither moral nor cost-effective</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper limit comparison</strong>: the Tang-Luo-style soul ring system is precisely the predatory soul ring path&#39;s typical case; commoners rely on ring gifts, geniuses rely on hunting, ceiling locked by birth; Path D replaces this path wholesale</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: Path D can mass-replicate and train Myriad Races, predatory path one life for one strong one, coverage under 99%</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: Path D&#39;s efficiency advantage comes from open sharing, not hoarding; the more open, the faster replication, the higher efficiency</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The predatory soul ring path is a downhill road &quot;tempting first half, dead end second half&quot;; Path D is an uphill road &quot;stable first half, open second half.&quot; Across the nine realms, the answer is not &quot;which is more passionate,&quot; but &quot;which road lets more people truly reach origin.&quot;</p><p>In the final analysis, Path D vs. predatory soul ring path realm-wide energy-level efficiency comparison described in this document is no isolated case — operating within Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s overall coordinates; its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./04-反掠夺主义核心论纲.html">04-Anti-Predation Core Treatise</a> · <a href="./181-D路线人族人造道则魂环.html">181-Path D Humanoid Artificial Dao-Rule Soul Rings</a> · <a href="./15-能量循环与转化法则.html">15-Energy Cycle and Transformation Law</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',24)])])}const p=t(n,[["render",r]]);export{g as __pageData,p as default};
